sequenceDiagram
  %% Production policy only. Development uses the independent Gateway precheck in container/deploy-default.mmd; this schedule and its persisted pause are never changed by that tick.
  %% Target design: DECISIONS 3 (automatic deploy = Gateway-published native schedule, no POST back), R1-R2, ADR 0244, behavior names by target. Replaces instance.policy_event. docs/reference/deployments.md#automatic-deployments.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 3, 5 (no per-minute Node read: the schedule inputs carry the deployed commit, and the Gateway republishes them on each deploy).
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: instance:auto-deploy:enable · Automatic deploys
  %% kind: instance.auto_deploy
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as app-prod Node<br/>Node 12 over ssh
  CLI->>GW: auto-deploy:enable 42<br/>orbit instance:auto-deploy:enable
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:auto-deploy:enable 42`
  %%> - syntax: `<instance>`; `instance:auto-deploy:disable <instance>` turns it off
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - turns automatic deployment on for production Instance 42
  %%> - also resumes an Instance that a manual deploy or rollback paused
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - deploys nothing now and changes nothing on the Node
  %%> Typical use:
  %%> - a production Instance follows `main`: merge a PR, CI turns green, the next fire deploys it
  Note over GW: Check, record auto-deploy<br/>Instance 42 · on, unpaused
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12
  %%> - Instance 42 is an active production Instance; before its first succeeded deployment the check reports `not_deployed`
  %%> - when the Project has a `merge_check`, the GitHub App can read its check runs
  %%> Result:
  %%> - auto-deploy recorded as on and unpaused
  GW->>SW: Publish the schedule<br/>auto-deploy-42 · every minute
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - publishes one native Swamp schedule for Instance 42
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - branch, `merge_check`, blocked commits, retry times
  %%> - the deployed commit; the Gateway republishes the inputs after each deploy or rollback
  %%> - vault key names for the read token; the Gateway keeps the token fresh in the vault
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the run has everything it needs; it never calls the Gateway
  GW-->>CLI: Enabled<br/>auto_deploy: on
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the Instance with auto-deploy on, at once
  %%> - no task: publishing the schedule is part of the command
  loop every minute, second 30
    Note over SW: tick
    %%> Native policy producer:
    %%> - the retained fleet policy selects work and produces the complete event receipt
    SW->>SW: Find newest green commit<br/>ls-remote · merge_check passed
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - reads the branch head with `git ls-remote`
    %%> - walks first-parent history to the newest commit whose `merge_check` passed
    %%> - skips blocked commits and commits whose retry isn't due
    %%> Not included:
    %%> - never deploys a red or pending commit
    %%> - compares with the deployed commit from the inputs; no SSH to the production Node each minute
    alt a newer green commit
      SW->>N: Deploy the pinned commit<br/>deploy-42 · prepare … check
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - the same steps as `instance:deploy`, pinned to the commit
      %%> - behavior `deploy-42`: one lock per Instance, so a manual deploy and a fire never overlap
      SW-->>GW: Fire ended<br/>result, commit, deployment
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - the result (`started`, `failed`, `gate_failed`, …), the commit and the deployment outputs
      Note over GW: Record the result<br/>history row · Activity · alert
      %%> Result:
      %%> - a deployment history row with origin `automatic`
      %%> - one Activity entry `auto_deploy.<result>` when the result changes
      %%> - a release alert for a failed deploy, a stalled commit or a pause
      %%> On failure:
      %%> - the commit is blocked, or gets a retry time (10, then 20 minutes)
      %%> - the Gateway republishes the schedule with the new inputs
    else nothing to deploy
      SW-->>GW: Fire ended<br/>up_to_date or gate_pending
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the Gateway updates the last result shown by `instance:show`
      %%> - no history row, no Activity entry
    end
  end
  Note over SW: failures
  %%> Native end check:
  %%> - the policy producer records zero failures on success
  %%> - the Gateway captures its full fire_json in the same terminal history read, including events from a failed fire
  %%> - no reporting shell forwards or prints the receipt
  Note over GW,SW: Pause<br/>manual deploy or rollback
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - a manual `instance:deploy` or `instance:rollback` pauses auto-deploy
  %%> - the Gateway removes the schedule's trigger; no fire runs
  %%> Resume:
  %%> - `orbit instance:auto-deploy:enable 42` publishes it again
  %%> Disable:
  %%> - `orbit instance:auto-deploy:disable 42` removes the schedule
